--TEST--
An `@throws` that names a class which is not an error is `E0334`, and a user class that extends `RuntimeError` is accepted — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `@throws` names an error class.
final class Entry {
}

final class LedgerClosed extends RuntimeError {
}

final class Ledger {
    /// Adds one entry.
    ///
    /// @throws Entry when the entry is wrong
    /// @throws LedgerClosed when the ledger is closed
    public static function add(int $amount): int {
        return $amount;
    }
}
echo Ledger::add(3), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0334]: `@throws` names `Entry`, which is not an error class
   --> %s:12:17
   |
12 |     /// @throws Entry when the entry is wrong
   |                 ^^^^^ not a class that extends `Throwable`
   = suggestion: delete the `@throws` line (delete)

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
